    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0348" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/1735: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-13T18:00:00-05:00">November 13, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>89. Second paragraph my telegram number 88, November 11, 10 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">9</hi>] a.m. Bill was passed Senate in third debate
                    Saturday and is now before House of Representatives. It provides also that
                    forced sale of mortgaged property shall not be effected unless bid received is
                    at least equal to appraised value of property. Provisions of law 37 of 1932
                    (despatch number 4806 of November 28, 1932<anchor n="47" xml:id="d215-f1"/>) and
                    of bill itself are extended to include mortgages held by insurance companies.
                    National City Bank has instructed its local manager to present energetic protest
                    and request assistance of the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
